-- title:
--   Equal dimensions for mod p cusp forms and glued differentials
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a non-zero natural number with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ containing every unit $u$ whose image under the reduction `ZMod.unitsMap` along $(M/p) \mid M$ is trivial, and let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, regarded as an algebra over $\mathbb{Z}/p$. Write $L =$ [`CuspForm.twoCuspLattice M H 2 p (⊥ : Subring ℂ)`](def/CuspForm_TwoCuspLattice.html#L86), the module over the smallest subring of $\mathbb{C}$ attached to weight-two forms of level $(M,H)$, and let [`CuspForm.IntTwoCuspForms M H p`](def/ModularCurve_XHDifferentialsModL.html#L374) be its quotient by the submodule $pL$; on the geometric side let $\Gamma =$ [`CohCarrier.GammaH (M/p) (ModularCurve.infSubgroup p M H hpM)`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), the image in $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ of the preimage in $\Gamma_0(M/p)$, under the determinantal character `gamma0Units`, of the image of $H$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^{\times}$, let $F =$ [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC K Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) be the intermediate field of $K$-Laurent series generated by the integral form ratios, and let [`ModularCurve.twoCompRegularDifferentials K Γ p`](def/ModularCurve_XHDifferentialsModL.html#L320) be the $K$-span, inside $\Omega[F/K] \times \Omega[F/K]$, of the glued polar pairs for the set of node pairs $(\mathrm{Frob}(v), v)$ with $v$ a supersingular place. The assertion is that $K \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}/p}$ `IntTwoCuspForms M H p` and this submodule are both finite-dimensional over $K$, and that their $K$-dimensions coincide.
--
--   This is the dimension count matching the mod $p$ reduction of the integral weight-two cusp-form lattice of level $\Gamma_H(M)$, with $p$ exactly dividing $M$, against the regular differentials of the two-component (Deligne–Rapoport) special fibre at level $\Gamma_{H'}(M/p)$, glued along the supersingular points. It is the numerical input for [`ModularCurve.exists_linearEquiv_intTwoCuspForms_twoCompRegularDifferentials`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_linearEquiv_intTwoCuspForms_twoCompRegularDifferentials), which upgrades the equality of dimensions to a linear isomorphism.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_finrank_tensorProduct_intTwoCuspForms_eq_finrank_twoCompRegularDifferentials.lean

